  "term": "control condition",
  "definition": "A control condition is the comparison group or situation in an independent-groups study that is used as a reference for judging the effects of an experimental manipulation. In the source passage, it is the non-manipulated comparison condition whose standard deviation may be used when the manipulation could change variability in the experimental group.",
